Please tell us why you find other roles/races difficult. Knights and
tourists are infinitely more succesful protection racketeers than
healers.

See http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Protection_racket#Race_and_Role

If I play somewhat conservative, I'll have a near 100% success with
knights and tourists going for 0 naked AC. That's not something you
can say for gnomish healers. There's just one possibility of failure
with those classes, namely losing your pet to a trap or to Minetown
guards.

With gnomish healers, you'll die of starvation fairly often. Not to
mention their cumpulsory start scumming for 5+ mana. BTW, you can
easily get 0 naked AC with a 2 or even 3 XL healer, so that scumming
is useless. Just get to 15+ mana to get loads of meatballs via stone
to flesh, and looting all shops will get you more than 12000 zordmiks.
Then again, you'll usually get those 12000 z with a XL 1 tourist or
knight, going for a superb -2 naked AC.

I don't find gnomish healers particularly better than human wizards at
the protection racket. And in the midgame, what would you rather have,
a 0 naked AC healer or a 0 naked AC wizard? Point in case:

